reasons={
'S16':'Manipulation hypothesis from handle/move repertoire, not unencumbered speed or turnover total.',
'S17':'Security hypothesis from explicit possession/turnover assessment. Without loss typing, cause and pressure exposure remain uncertain; no AST/TOV-to-grade formula.',
'S18':'Space-making craft hypothesis from isolation/shot creation or explicit separation limitation; shot accuracy and physical acceleration separate.',
'S19':'Driving-angle/pace craft hypothesis from paint access or pressure limits, not the finish conversion itself; tools/context remain confounded.',
'S20':'Broad action-choice hypothesis from stabilizing decisions/orchestration or limited self-creation. Specific pass windows stay in F fields; scoring skill is not counted again.',
'S33':'On-ball technique hypothesis from creator assignment/containment or defensive targeting, conditional on movement tools; overall defense cannot isolate exact technique.',
'S34':'Contact/leverage hypothesis from physical POA or switching success. Strength/mass is not added again as raw technique.',
'S38':'Help/rotation recognition hypothesis; helper effectiveness includes recognition and travel and cannot isolate the former precisely.',
'S39':'Off-ball starting-position hypothesis from positioning/help coverage or off-ball weakness, correlated with S38 but not an independent observation.',
'S40':'Arrival-control hypothesis from positioning/pressure, weakly identified; no timed closeout or travel-speed observation.',
'S41':'Anticipation hypothesis from explicit anticipation/hands/coverage description; steal/block counts alone do not identify it.',
'S44':'Attention/responsibility hypothesis from sustained positioning or off-ball lapses. Not personality, effort, intelligence or a proven causal breakdown count.',
'S45':'Broad foul-control concern from explicit foul-rate criticism; foul types/intentions/assignment exposure unknown; does not prove all fouls are technique errors.'}
pair_reasons={
'Luka Dončić':'Every-pass/P&R orchestration supports broad window recognition and delivery. Wider/lower lob delivery ranges reflect route precision not independently observed; midpoint differences are judgment, not established read-versus-execution defect.',
'Shai Gilgeous-Alexander':'P&R plus improving playmaking supports roll/kick hypotheses below the clearest scoring/security anchors; no evidence separates recognition from delivery, so their ranges intentionally match.',
'Jalen Brunson':'High-level scorer with comparatively limited engine passing; simple kick competence plausible. Matching recognition/delivery reflects absence of a supported split.',
'Cade Cunningham':'High-load creation with substantial turnovers: broad read competence plus uncertain pressured delivery. Execution midpoint below recognition is a TESTABLE attribution hypothesis; loss type could instead implicate handling or decisions and reverse it.',
'Darius Garland':'Explicit passing/P&R and engine praise supports roll/kick reads/deliveries. Small range offset is a weak judgment, not a measured split; healthy state assumed.',
'Dylan Harper':'Advanced read development explicitly remains open despite stable decisions/security. Simple-window delivery may be stronger than advanced recognition; overlap is wide and no isolated pass sample proves the split.',
'Desmond Bane':'Passing praised as a secondary option, so connector pair only. Pressure/separation failures do not automatically become poor pass delivery.',
'Stephon Castle':'Useful secondary playmaking but turnover concern; connector pair only, no invented route-specific cause of losses.',
'Derrick White':'Good decisions/passing/low losses support connector and simple kick competence; primary drive access remains separate and restricted.',
'Scottie Barnes':'Elite passing and lead-creator growth support connector/kick hypotheses; slight delivery offset is uncertain decomposition, not direct misdelivery evidence. No automatic all-family elite grid.',
'Bam Adebayo':'Generic playmaking/creation supports a broad connector pair, not independently identified lob/roll/kick subskills.'}
